Subject: [PATCH 27/28] B70: product answers in plain language, 400-800 words

Product answers echoed the synthesis prompt's internal vocabulary: 17 of 20
answers in the 2026-10-08 02:20 run said "the supplied evidence", "the
packet" or "the provided material". They ran 3,000-12,000 characters under a
2,000-word cap. The quality-first system prompt now tells the model to write
for the person who asked, never mention the packet, rows, controller or
pipeline, refer to sources by publisher or page, and aim for 400-800 words
(never more than 1,200), with one short paragraph or list per option.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 agent/quality_first_route.py | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/agent/quality_first_route.py b/agent/quality_first_route.py
index a8ec5f0..700b97a 100644
--- a/agent/quality_first_route.py
+++ b/agent/quality_first_route.py
@@ -217,7 +217,14 @@ historical price cannot pass a hard current-price cap.
 Give the conclusion first. Explain material uncertainty and evidence gaps. Cite every
 factual paragraph with normal Markdown links using only the exact allowed URLs. Never
 emit a tool call, receipt command, publication claim, or hidden process commentary.
-Return a finished answer of at most 2,000 words."""
+
+Write for the person who asked, in plain language. The evidence packet, its rows, the
+controller and the pipeline are internal: never mention them, and never write phrases
+such as "the supplied evidence", "the provided evidence", "the packet" or "the provided
+material". Refer to sources by publisher or page instead ("Hisense's product page",
+"RTINGS' review", "the sources I found"). Keep it tight: aim for 400-800 words, never
+more than 1,200, with one short paragraph or bullet list per option and no repeated
+caveats."""
 
 
 def synthesis_messages(
